Cell["\<\
Parameters : tau = 5, T = 6, Nd = 12, sigma = 0.02, Bmax = 8
nseeds = 10\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9868878888099546`*^9, 
  3.986887911371634*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"084e32c8-9e2c-4dc7-a584-\
dc35d75de77f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Reconstruction performance",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "\nThe reconstruction tests are run with the same physical parameters and \
the same number of noise realizations for each latent dimension, so the \
reported mean_RMSE values from recon_test.py are directly comparable. Lower \
mean_RMSE means better reconstruction.\n\nTo plot a higher-is-better score, \
the RMSE values are normalized by the worst RMSE among the currently tested \
latent dimensions:\n\n",
 StyleBox["reconstruction performance = 1 - meanRMSE/rmseRef",
  Background->RGBColor[0.93, 0.27, 0.27, 0.33]],
 ",\n\nwhere rmseRef = Max[Join[meanRMSE, meanRMSEcpu]]. With this \
definition, performance = 1 would correspond to perfect reconstruction, while \
performance = 0 corresponds to the worst model in the current comparison set. \
For example, a value of 0.47 means that the model reduces the reconstruction \
RMSE by about 47% relative to the current worst model."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.986889*^9, 3.98688862944072*^9}, 3.9868887138770447`*^9},
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.75, 0, 0.33],ExpressionUUID->"0fb3589e-32fa-4b7d-aea5-4fd2e22556cc"],

